    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "権利 primarily means 'right' or 'entitlement' and does not fully capture the nuance of 'privilege' as a special advantage, immunity, or unearned benefit. While JMdict lists 'privilege' as a gloss for 権利, it is not the most natural or comprehensive translation for a general learner across all contexts of 'privilege'. For 'privilege' in the sense of a special advantage, 特権 (tokken) is a more direct and natural fit. For 'privilege' as an honor or pleasure (e.g., 'It was a privilege to meet you'), 光栄 (kōei) would be more appropriate.",
